{"title":"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit integer less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> where each digit is odd and the sum of the cubes of the digits is\nthe original number.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have a three digit number that can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc46375ebb5ca6566960b9ea085bace5976d5321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1bc$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"13\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are odd, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/1/dd13230ed7905340c41f783f7c4be7d51c95e04d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b^3 + c^3 + 1 = 100 + 10b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"214\" height=\"16\" />. This means that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are within the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/445a5ca77814f995fd9f43c452f7a628cc34b1ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1,3,5,7,9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />. We also notice that since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd99228146175c61e5cca6be965d17c918d45cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/a/27a5fa245729edc3c72a7294ddb5d6b3c28541a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> are both far greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, they can not be our digits, so the remaining set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c9a1534884181fdf5971f6ec19b8d02adfb07c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1,3,5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. Looking at only the last digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296264ceaa0451bdf7b2be3ccf9b5823fbd48e10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^3 = 1, 3^3 = 27, 5^3 = 125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"192\" height=\"18\" />, we see that only when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are together can we get a last digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which we see is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/3/d332fb07d4b82068c7853ec5642654061ebbf0a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125+27+1 = 153$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"14\" />. Upon checking, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/80750543da9b7dfc4c1242ecb64d820a9b091577.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{153}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"40\" height=\"22\" /> is a working solution.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II\">2010 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_Northern_Colorado_Math_Contest\" title=\"University of Northern Colorado Math Contest\"> All UNCO Math Contest Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017223445\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 154/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1363/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 100/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3482/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.998      1 Template:UNCO_Math_Contest_box\n100.00%    6.998      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13486:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017223445 and revision id 67763. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}